"Another fine candidate," the king of the underground tells Daren, his gaze flicking to Reidzek to take measure of the man. "Doctor Reidzek has earned immense respect in the short time he has spent among us. He would draw a considerable share of the vote if he chose to stand. What do you say, Doctor? Shall I put your name on the ballot?"

"I... must decline," Reidzek says, raising both hands. "Forgive me, Daren, but the crown is too heavy a burden for a simple craftsman. I threw my lot in with this rebellion to mend what was broken in the city, not to govern an entire realm. I hope that does not disappoint you."

"No, not at all," Daren says, stepping back. "It is your choice. I only meant to put the thought forward..."

