ID: B3-Ch08b-Kelrim
TEXT:

set(v_b3_ch8_king,5)
 "If a trustworthy king is what you're looking for, then Kelrim would be my choice."

"The goblin?" The king of the underground freezes, genuinely caught off guard. "A goblin ruling Ollendor? That is... an unprecedented nomination. We can record it, of course, but... does anyone else have a suggestion?"

"I stand behind Kelrim as well," Daren says firmly. "He has every quality of a worthy ruler."

"Did I hear that correctly?" Kelrim hurries over, his green ears twitching. "Daren, did you just propose me for the throne?"

"Barry put the name forward first, but I agree with him completely," Daren says.

"I am grateful for your faith in me," Kelrim says, looking between the two of us, "but a goblin reigning over a city of humans is unheard of. I am already indebted to the people of Ollendor for letting our kind take shelter within these walls. Claiming the crown feels like abusing their hospitality. Beyond the two of you, who would ever cast a vote for me? I am sorry, but--"

"I will give you my vote!" a booming voice cuts across the hall. The heavy oak door to the quarantine ward swings shut behind an imposing figure.

His clothes hang in rags, and his knees tremble under his weight, yet a commanding stillness sits in his broad shoulders and unyielding eyes.

"Brother, what are you doing out of bed?" Desmond shouts from the threshold, dropping his guard stance. "You are still recovering!"

"Nonsense," the man grunts, limping forward one painful step at a time. "Sound as a bell."

"Desmond's brother?" I murmur to Daren. "How is he on his feet? He was dying yesterday."

"I have no explanation," Daren whispers back. "I have witnessed remarkable recoveries, but never on this scale. Standing in his condition takes raw willpower."

"How much of our talk reached you in the ward?" Albert asks as the wounded man nears. "Have you been listening at the keyhole?"

"Not the entire time," the man says, coming to a halt beside Kelrim and planting a heavy hand on Daren's shoulder for support. "I meant to give my younger brother a fright by walking out on my own two feet, but your discussion caught my ear. I had no intention of stepping in until these travelers put our good healer forward for the throne. At that point, staying quiet was out of the question."

"Is that Sir Horace?" a voice calls from the crowd. "By the gods, he lives! Sir Horace is alive!"

"It is him!" another shouts. "Praise the gods, he survived!"

"Sir Horace has returned to us!" a third cry rings out.

choice("Continue", B3-Ch08b-Kelrim2, v_current_scene = B3-Ch08b-Kelrim2)


ID: B3-Ch08b-King2
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch6_kelrim == 1 && v_b3_ch8_king != 4 || v_b3_ch6_plan == 3 && v_b3_ch8_king != 4) {
 "Do you have anyone else to put forward?" the king asks Daren.

"What about Desmond?" Daren ventures. "He strikes me as someone who could--"

"Leave me out of your politics!" Desmond bellows from the quarantine doorway. "I took this guard post so I would never have to take high-stakes risks again. If you think you can push a crown onto my head, you have lost your mind."

"No one is forcing you," Daren says quickly. "We are only weighing possibilities."

"Desmond declines as well," the king of the underground says. "Does another name come to mind?"

"I was thinking perhaps..."

Daren glances toward Kelrim, hesitating. With Reidzek and Desmond both recoiling from the prospect, he hesitates to corner his friend. He scans the torchlit hall for another prospect, then lets his shoulders drop in defeat.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_kelrim != 1 && v_b3_ch6_plan != 3 || v_b3_ch8_king == 4) {
 "Do you have anyone else to put forward?" the king asks Daren.

"What about Desmond?" Daren ventures. "He strikes me as someone who could--"

"Leave me out of your politics!" Desmond bellows from the quarantine doorway. "I took this guard post so I would never have to take high-stakes risks again. If you think you can push a crown onto my head, you have lost your mind."

"No one is forcing you," Daren says quickly. "We are only weighing possibilities."

"Desmond declines as well," the king of the underground says. "Does another name come to mind?"

"I was thinking perhaps..."

Daren searches the faces in the waiting hall, hunting for anyone suited to wear a crown, before bowing his head in resignation.

}
#if(v_b3_ch8_king == 0) {
 "Finding the right individual for such a burden is no simple task," the king of the underground tells Daren. "Rare is the soul possessing the resolve, leadership, and willingness to shoulder an entire realm. Rest assured, our election will be fair, and your friend's nomination will appear on the ballot—provided the candidate accepts."

The king turns to Albert, waiting.

"If it serves your purpose, my king," Albert says, a flicker of uncertainty crossing his features. "I will stand."

"Splendid," the king of the underground says. "With that resolved, shall we turn to the matter of the Overseer, or did you have further inquiries for me?"

"One more thing," Kate says. "What do you intend to do with the prisoners inside the seredium towers once the Overseer is broken?"

"Free them, naturally," the king of the underground says. "We must first neutralize the garrisons at the perimeter, of course, but as soon as--"

}
#if(v_b3_ch8_king == 1) {
 "Finding the right individual for such a burden is no simple task," the king of the underground tells Daren. "Rare is the soul possessing the resolve, leadership, and willingness to shoulder an entire realm. Rest assured, our election will be fair, and your friend's nomination will appear on the ballot—provided the candidate accepts."

The king turns to Peter, waiting.

"If the people believe in me," Peter says, visibly surprised to be asked, "I will not step back from the duty."

"Splendid," the king of the underground says. "With that resolved, shall we turn to the matter of the Overseer, or did you have further inquiries for me?"

